I don’t have direct access to the VirusTotal API from here, but here’s exactly what you’d need to call to get the **subdomain** descriptors for `example.org`:

```http
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/relationships/subdomains?limit=10&continuation_cursor=abc
Authorization: Bearer my_api
```

**What this returns**

The response will contain an array of objects, each with:

- `id` – the unique identifier for the subdomain object  
- `context_attributes` – any additional metadata that VirusTotal attaches to the relationship (e.g., first seen, last seen, etc.)

Only those two fields will be present; all other attributes are omitted per your request. If you hit the API yourself, you’ll see something like:

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "subdomain1.example.org",
      "context_attributes": { ... }
    },
    {
      "id": "subdomain2.example.org",
      "context_attributes": { ... }
    },
    ...
  ],
  "meta": { ... }
}
```

Feel free to replace `my_api` with your actual API key and adjust the `limit` or `continuation_cursor` as needed.
